  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence to exploit; the priority is establishing a clean, interpretable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest standard configuration: PCA is the most widely used and reproducible RNA dimensionality reduction, single-profile avoids confounding from aggregation, and RNA-only avoids confounding from fusion. This experiment establishes (1) whether the RNA signal alone is informative for the task, (2) a performance floor against which all image-only, multimodal, and alternative-encoder configurations can be compared, and (3) a reference for how much value the more complex design choices (scvi, scgpt, multiprofile, image, fusion) actually add. Under a limited budget, anchoring the search with the most standard, low-risk baseline maximizes the interpretability of every subsequent comparison and reduces uncertainty about whether the task is solvable from RNA at all before investing experiments in more complex modalities or encoders."
}

